From 3f0b191291ebb917211e03daf798daefae2e76e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:00:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(init): keep the fw4 include files of homeproxy in place

The uci-defaults of the package always add three fw4 includes:
homeproxy_forward, homeproxy_input and homeproxy_post. firewall_pre.uc
writes fw4_forward.nft and fw4_input.nft only when there are rules (the
TUN mode, an enabled server), and fw4_post.nft is not written without a
client node. For a file that does not exist fw4 prints "specifies
unreachable path ..., ignoring section" on every reload.

start_service now creates the three files empty before the generators
fill them, so the includes always point to a file and an empty one
changes nothing. This also drops stale rules of a previous mode.

Checked with the real rc.common of OpenWrt and stubs: after start in the
redirect mode the three files exist and are empty, in the TUN mode the
forward and input files get their rules, and stop leaves them empty.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011cyCFAA9hPeqN8wsgkxbrJ
---
diff --git a/root/etc/init.d/homeproxy b/root/etc/init.d/homeproxy
index b683af0..34c5a4a 100755
--- a/root/etc/init.d/homeproxy
+++ b/root/etc/init.d/homeproxy
@@ -273,6 +273,15 @@ start_service() {
 	chown -R sing-box:sing-box "$RUN_DIR"
 
 	# Setup firewall
+	# The uci-defaults of the package always add the fw4 includes
+	# homeproxy_forward, homeproxy_input and homeproxy_post. For a file that
+	# does not exist fw4 prints "specifies unreachable path ..., ignoring
+	# section" on every reload, and firewall_pre.uc writes its files only
+	# when there are rules (TUN, server). Start from empty files, the
+	# generators below fill them.
+	: > "$RUN_DIR/fw4_forward.nft"
+	: > "$RUN_DIR/fw4_input.nft"
+	: > "$RUN_DIR/fw4_post.nft"
 	ucode "$HP_DIR/scripts/firewall_pre.uc"
 	[ "$outbound_node" = "nil" ] || utpl -S "$HP_DIR/scripts/firewall_post.ut" > "$RUN_DIR/fw4_post.nft"
 	fw4 reload >"/dev/null" 2>&1
